' The browser shell's stage set -- the CEF half.
'
' This template is a DELTA over `packages`: check_examples.mjs's TEMPLATE_BASE
' names the base, and only the files that differ live here. The one that
' differs is this one.
'
' Why a template of its own, rather than one more block in the shared stage:
' Tutorials/CEF/Building a browser shell.md and its WebView2 twin are the same
' application written against two different browser controls, and both say
' "Drop a control onto a Form and rename it `WebView`". One name, two types, on
' pages that would otherwise share a project -- so no single stage set can
' carry it. The templates split, the name does not.
'
' Not WithEvents. A handler binds to a WithEvents variable declared in the SAME
' module, and every sample is generated into a module of its own, so a
' WithEvents here would bind nothing -- the two samples that are event handlers
' report TB5019 either way and are excerpts rather than programs.

Module tbxStageBrowser

    Public WebView As CefBrowser
    Public WebViewPreview As CefBrowser

    Public AddressBar As TextBox

    Public btnBack As CommandButton
    Public btnForward As CommandButton
    Public btnRefresh As CommandButton
    Public btnZoomIn As CommandButton
    Public btnZoomOut As CommandButton
    Public btnPDF As CommandButton
    Public btnDevTools As CommandButton

End Module
